        "id": "B0wnGmpNmcAT"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. The question: decision, action, cost of a wrong call\n",
        "\n",
        "*What decision does your work improve? Who acts on it? What does a wrong recommendation cost?*"
      ],
      "id": "B0wnGmpNmcAT"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The decision I want to improve is which pages a content editor should review first when investigating low click-through rates. The editor could use observed patterns in CTR across content types and search-position tiers to identify areas worth investigating, rather than automatically rewriting pages based on a single metric. A wrong recommendation could waste editing time on pages that do not need changes or divert attention from pages with more significant opportunities. I will begin with grouped comparisons and descriptive analysis to determine whether the patterns are consistent enough to justify further investigation. At this stage, the goal is decision support, not an automated model or a causal explanation."
      ],
