      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Quick look at the data (2-3 real numbers)\n",
        "\n",
        "*Load the starter CSV below and show 2-3 real numbers that make your lane look worth the next 7 weeks.*"
      ],
      "id": "VqICp9EVmcAY"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The starter dataset contains 30,000 rows and 44 columns. The correlation between search volume and impressions over 90 days was approximately 0.001, indicating almost no linear relationship between these two variables across the full dataset. Among the 22,006 pages with at least 100 impressions, mean CTR varied across search-position tiers. For example, mean CTR was approximately 0.3548% for `page_1` and 0.0554% for `deep`, using the dataset's percentage units. These are preliminary descriptive findings, not proof of what causes CTR differences. They provide a useful starting point for investigating which content groups may deserve further review."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "m3q0r7hPoNl8"
      },
      "id": "m3q0r7hPoNl8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "url = (\n",
        "    \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/\"\n",
        "    \"safiyakhan46/flyrank-ml-internship-starter/\"\n",
        "    \"main/data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(url)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Dataset shape:\", df.shape)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Discovery 1: relationship between search volume and impressions\n",
        "corr = df[\"search_volume\"].corr(df[\"impressions_90d\"])\n",
        "print(f\"Search volume vs. impressions correlation: {corr:.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Discovery 2: compare CTR across position tiers\n",
        "visible = df[df[\"impressions_90d\"] >= 100].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "summary = (\n",
        "    visible.groupby(\"position_tier\")[\"ctr\"]\n",
        "    .agg([\"mean\", \"count\"])\n",
        "    .sort_values(\"mean\", ascending=False)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nMean CTR by position tier (dataset percentage units):\")\n",
        "print(summary.round(4).to_string())\n"
